    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 3,
    "sentence": "For a fixed \\( j \\geq 2 \\), the inner sum is a geometric series: \\[\n\\sum_{k=2}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{j^k} = \\frac{1}{j^2} + \\frac{1}{j^3} + \\frac{1}{j^4} + \\cdots = \\frac{\\frac{1}{j^2}}{1 - \\frac{1}{j}} = \\frac{1}{j(j-1)}.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 4,
    "sentence": "Thus, the original sum becomes: \\[\n\\sum_{j=2}^{2008} \\frac{1}{j(j-1)}.",
